// RESTORE: packages/darklang/cli/registry.dark
// WAS: the help categories that `commandGroups ()` listed for commands the molt removed, and the
//      per-group entries it lost out of the groups that stayed.
// ANCHOR: `commandGroups ()` is still there, just above the completion helpers; these are entries
//      within its list, in this order.
// ALSO: registry.dark.sync, registry.dark.apps, registry.dark.auth, registry.dark.db,
//       registry.dark.scripts, registry.dark.squash and registry.dark.agent carry the command ROWS
//       themselves. This fragment is only the help grouping, which an earlier version of
//       registry.dark.sync pointed at as `registry.dark.sync-groups`, a file that was never
//       written. This is that file, under a name that covers every round rather than just sync.
// WHEN: written 2026-10-12, covering every round of the molt
//
// Four whole groups went, because every command in them went:

      ("Sync", [ "sync", "push", "pull", "connect", "review", "whoami", "identity", "backups" ])
      ("AI", [ "agent" ])
      ("Network", [ "devices" ])
      ("Apps", [ "apps" ])

// And these entries left groups that stayed:
//
//   "Packages"   lost "db"
//   "Changes"    lost "squash"
//   "Execution"  lost "scripts"
//   "Utilities"  lost "views"
//
// Note that "backups" was in the Sync group and the `backups` COMMAND stayed, so restoring the
// Sync group verbatim is wrong: `backups` has to stay wherever the molt put it, or it ends up
// listed twice.
